>> title: Ginger-Garlic Paste
>> category: Spice Blends & Marinades
>> tags: indian, ginger, garlic, base, condiment
>> counters: Curry House
>> aka: adrak lehsun paste, ginger garlic paste, adrak lasun, GG paste
>> pairs-with: onion-tomato-masala
>> servings: 1 cup
>> time: 15 min
>> step.1: peel and blitz to a rough paste
>> step.2: work in, blitz smooth
>> step.3: pack down, film with oil, into the fridge

Blitz @fresh ginger{4%oz}(115 g; peel it by scraping with a teaspoon) and @garlic{4%oz}(115 g; peeled) in a #small food processor{} to a rough paste.

Work @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @neutral oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL) into @&(~1)paste{} and blitz smooth. The salt is what keeps it from going grey by Thursday and the oil is what stops it climbing the blade.

Pack @&(~1)paste{} into a clean #jar{}, film the top with @neutral oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL) and put it in the fridge. It keeps three weeks under the oil, and it is ready the moment it is blended — the wait is how long the jar lasts, not how long the paste takes. Equal weights is the house ratio; two parts garlic to one of ginger is the other one, and both are on menus. Two tablespoons is one curry.
